            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SoCalAngel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a nice recipe for brunch or even dinner! Here are some tips for making this: *Use very good quality smoked salmon. You can sprinkle with dried dill, if you don’t have fresh. Stir the boiling water to create a whirlpool before dropping egg in. This will create a nicely shaped poached egg. Cook eggs one at a time, boil for about 1.5 to 2 minutes in boiling water, the eggs should be soft and have a runny yolk. Make with the Microwave Hollandaise Sauce from this site.",
            "datePublished": "2022-07-06T22:35:15.521Z"
          },
